{#
  Gel Overlay Atom - SVG-masked background element with corner manipulation

  ARCHITECTURE:
  - gel.njk: Renders DOM element with ID and color class
  - Gel.js: Controls SVG polygon mask and corner animation
  - GelAnimationManager: Initializes and coordinates multiple gels on scroll
  - GelManipulator: Positions gel relative to viewport or reference element

  ELEMENT IDS AND CONFIGURATION:
  - Element ID must match arrangement keys used by gel choreography (e.g., id="bg-gel-0")
  - IDs use kebab-case format: bg-gel-0, bg-gel-1, bg-gel-2
  - .gel class triggers automatic discovery during initialization
  - Color classes (gel-primary, etc.) set the gradient's base colour
  - Direction classes (gel-top, gel-bottom-left, etc.) set where it goes "to"; default is top
  - Fade classes (gel-fade-xs … gel-fade-xl, gel-fade-full) set how far the gradient travels; default is full
  - Colour, direction and fade only set variables read by .gel, so they combine in any order (see styles/backgrounds/Gel.css)

  USAGE:
  {% import "atoms/gel.njk" as gelAtom %}
  {{ gelAtom.render({ color: 'gel-primary', id: 'bg-gel-0' }) }}

  PARAMETERS:
  - color: CSS classes for color, direction and fade (default: 'gel-primary'), e.g. 'gel-primary gel-top gel-fade-md'
  - id: Element ID matching gel arrangement entries (required for choreography)
#}
{% macro render(params = {}) %}
  {%- set color = params.color | default('gel-primary') -%}
  {%- set id = params.id | default('gel-default') -%}

  <div id="{{ id }}"
       class="gel absolute inset-0 {{ color }}"
       aria-hidden="true"></div>

{% endmacro %}
